
==========================================================================
  dist_l NATURALITY PROBE  (documentation of LIMITATIONS §6)
==========================================================================

  This probe DOCUMENTS the current-implementation behavior
  described in docs/LIMITATIONS.md §6.  It does not assert
  correctness; it reports what the compiler actually does.

  P_L = (id_{A⊕B} ⊗ X_C) ; dist_l(A, B, C)
  P_R = dist_l(A, B, C) ; [ (id_A ⊗ X_C) ⊕ (id_B ⊗ X_C) ]

  Both : (A ⊕ B) ⊗ C  →  (A ⊗ C) ⊕ (B ⊗ C)
  Wires: 4 (tag 1 + payload 2 + C 1);  4 (tag 1 + payload 3).
  Valid codewords: 4 + 8 = 12 of 16 basis states.

==========================================================================
  PART 1: Compile P_L with materialize=False (symbolic wire perms)
==========================================================================

4 qubits, 1 gates
  X q[3]
  perm: [0, 1, 2, 3]

==========================================================================
  PART 2: Compile P_R with materialize=False (symbolic wire perms)
==========================================================================

4 qubits, 6 gates
  ToffoliBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  X q[0]
  CX q[0, 2]
  X q[0]
  CX q[0, 3]
  ToffoliBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  perm: [0, 1, 2, 3]

==========================================================================
  PART 3: Compile P_L with materialize=True (SWAPs emitted)
==========================================================================

4 qubits, 1 gates
  X q[3]
  perm: [0, 1, 2, 3]

==========================================================================
  PART 4: Compile P_R with materialize=True (SWAPs emitted)
==========================================================================

4 qubits, 6 gates
  ToffoliBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  X q[0]
  CX q[0, 2]
  X q[0]
  CX q[0, 3]
  ToffoliBox q[0, 1, 2, 3]
  perm: [0, 1, 2, 3]

==========================================================================
  PART 5: Observed unitary equality  (Bridge.eq_circ, materialize=True)
==========================================================================

  Bridge.eq_circ compiles both terms with materialize=True and
  compares full 2^4 = 16-dim unitaries, including 12 valid
  codewords + 4 padding basis states.

  Observed: P_L = P_R   (fidelity = 1.000000)

  Full agreement observed. This indicates the layout-frame
  repair (see docs/LAYOUT_FRAME_REPAIR.md) has landed
  or the incompleteness has otherwise been resolved.
  Please update docs/LIMITATIONS.md §6 accordingly.

==========================================================================
  END OF PROBE
==========================================================================

  This file exits 0 on both the documented behavior (fidelity 0.5)
  and the post-repair behavior (fidelity 1.0). A change of behavior
  is signalled by a diff against the committed .output file, not by
  a test-runner failure.
